  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "For Copeland's polynomial-content conjecture (OEIS A131758, revision 48, COMMENTS block signed September 9, 2008), we determine every row content using Carlitz's polynomial congruence (1953/54, Theorem 3, equation (4.8)). The content is 1 at indices 0, 1 and all even indices, and 2 at every odd index at least 3. This replaces the proposed divisor-count formula; every index 6s+8, s>=0, also excludes its one-place shift. The proof identifies content with a fixed divisor of an integer Laguerre polynomial. Direct proofs of associated transform identities and normalization corrections are included.",
